## Step-by-Step Implementation

### 1. Model Evaluation & Promotion

Evaluated candidate runs in the `fraud-detection-v2` experiment using the MLflow SDK, queried for the top `f1_score`, registered the model artifact as `fraud-detector-v2`, and assigned the `champion` alias to version `1`.

```python
import mlflow
from mlflow.tracking import MlflowClient

client = MlflowClient()

# Fetch target experiment
exp = client.get_experiment_by_name("fraud-detection-v2")

# Retrieve top candidate sorted by f1_score
runs = client.search_runs(
    experiment_ids=[exp.experiment_id],
    order_by=["metrics.f1_score DESC"],
    max_results=1
)
top_run = runs[0]

# Register top run and set alias
model_uri = f"runs:/{top_run.info.run_id}/model"
reg_model = mlflow.register_model(model_uri, "fraud-detector-v2")
client.set_registered_model_alias(
    name="fraud-detector-v2",
    alias="champion",
    version=reg_model.version
)
2. Model Serving
Served the promoted champion version locally on port 5001 in the background:

Bash
export MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI="http://localhost:5000"

nohup mlflow models serve \
  -m "models:/fraud-detector-v2@champion" \
  --port 5001 \
  --host 0.0.0.0 \
  --env-manager local > /tmp/mlflow_serve.log 2>&1 &
3. Monitoring & Health Check
Created /root/code/monitor.sh to probe the served endpoint and report health status.

monitor.sh
Bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash

HTTP_STATUS=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}" http://localhost:5001/health)

if [ "$HTTP_STATUS" -eq 200 ]; then
    exit 0
else
    exit 1
fi
Make executable and run validation:

Bash
chmod +x /root/code/monitor.sh
/root/code/monitor.sh && echo "Health check passed!"
Verification Summary
Check Point	Command / Metric	Expected Result	Status
